WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.282
"The Benefits of Black and Green Teas for Brain Waves"

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.520
Tea—whether white tea,
green tea, oolong, or black—

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.920
are all made
from the tea plant,

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.480
Camellia sinensis.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.240
That's different
from herbal tea,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.760
which is defined
as pouring hot water

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.880
over any plant in the world

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.080
other than
this particular plant.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:29.360
There are at least 287,655
different plants

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.840
that we know of on this planet.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.000
Why is this one plant

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.160
the most popular beverage
in the world?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.440
It's not the caffeine;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.120
the coffee plant
has more caffeine,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.480
but more people drink tea
than coffee.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.320
It's probably not the taste;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.800
most people would
probably prefer peppermint

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.960
or some of the fruity
berry teas

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.320
to be better tasting.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:51.920
It's a pretty enough plant,

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.440
but why do we drink literally
billions of cups a day

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.520
of this particular plant?

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.920
It turns out
there's something in this plant

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.800
that's found concentrated
in only two places in nature—

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.240
in the tea plant
and in an odd mushroom

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.680
called the bay bolete,

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.640
which has these little holes
instead of gills.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.200
Scientists figured this one
might not pair as well

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.160
with crumpets,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.360
so they called the compound
theanine.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.440
What does it do
that's got billions of people

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.160
hooked on it?

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.360
We weren't quite sure

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.360
until we hooked people up
to an EEG.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.760
An electroencephalogram
measures the activity

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.360
of our brain waves,

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.520
which are split
into four major bandwidths:

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.640
we have delta waves,
theta waves,

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.280
alpha waves, and beta waves.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.840
Delta waves,
where basically our brain

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.080
is electrically pulsing
very slowly

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.000
at about a wave per second,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.920
are seen primarily
in deep sleep.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.160
Then there are theta waves—

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.960
at about five cycles
per second—

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.560
typically seen
when we're drowsy

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.320
or in early sleep.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.360
The two waking states
are alpha and beta.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.080
We have alpha brain waves
when we're relaxed,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.120
aware, attentive,

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.600
like when we close our eyes
and meditate.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.960
And beta waves are more
when we're stimulated

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.360
with increased alertness,
in a hustle-and-bustle state

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.440
where most of us
live our lives.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.080
How can we get more
in that alpha state,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.840
that wakeful relaxation,

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.720
fully alert and focused
but calm?

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.680
Well, if we relax
in a nice peaceful place,

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.840
after about 90 minutes
we can start to see

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.240
some significant
alpha activity,

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.240
which is this yellow and red.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.920
Now, practicing meditators,
like Buddhist monks,

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.680
can achieve this state earlier,

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.000
and even maintain
alpha activity

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.520
with their eyes open.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:39.120
And the deeper the meditation,
the higher the alpha waves.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.920
So, we can meditate
for 30 years

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.240
or just drink some tea.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.840
This was the alpha wave
activity

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:51.200
in the control group
after drinking plain water.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.720
What if, instead of water,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.160
they had the amount of theanine

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.320
found in one or two cups
(240 to 480 ml) of tea?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.240
Look closely, compare, and see

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.040
if you can detect a difference.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:07.947
That is why people drink tea
from the tea plant.

